cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "lean-misc-math: miscellaneous mathematical results formalised in Lean 4"
message: >-
  If you use these results in your work, please cite this repository. Selection and
  curation of the results, and a best-effort read of each statement, are the author's
  contribution; the Lean statements and proofs are machine-generated and
  machine-verified, and the proofs are read by nobody. See README.md.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Constantinides
    given-names: George A.
    alias: geoconuk
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0201-310X"
repository-code: "https://github.com/geoconuk/lean-misc-math"
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 library of miscellaneous classical and other mathematical results built on
  Mathlib. The choice of which results to formalise, how they should be stated, and
  which are worth publishing is the author's contribution, as is a best-effort read of
  each Lean statement against its informal claim. The Lean statements and their proofs
  are generated by Claude; the proofs are read by nobody. Both are checked by Lean's
  kernel and audited so that every declaration depends only on propext,
  Classical.choice and Quot.sound. A best-effort read of a statement is not a review,
  and users should verify that a statement says what they need before relying on it.
keywords:
  - Lean 4
  - Mathlib
  - formalised mathematics
  - interactive theorem proving
  - machine-generated proofs
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-08-08"
